{"name":"Close but No Cigar","hex":"#361d0a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"close but no cigar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["Alternative form of close, but no cigar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/close_but_no_cigar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Close but No Cigar (Thomas Dolby song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Close but No Cigar\" is a song by English singer and musician Thomas Dolby, released by Virgin Records on 27 April 1992 as the lead single from his fourth studio album, Astronauts & Heretics (1992). The song, which was written and produced by Dolby, reached number 22 on the UK singles chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/90/Thomas_Dolby_Close_but_No_Cigar_1992_single_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Close_but_No_Cigar_(Thomas_Dolby_song)"},{"title":"Straight Outta Lynwood","blocks":[{"text":"Straight Outta Lynwood is the twelfth studio album by the American parody musician \"Weird Al\" Yankovic, released on September 26, 2006, the title drawing inspiration from hip hop group N.W.A's Straight Outta Compton. It was the sixth studio album self-produced by Yankovic. The musical styles on the album are built around parodies and pastiches of pop and rock music of the mid-2000s. The album's lead single, \"White & Nerdy\", is a parody of Chamillionaire's hit single \"Ridin'\". The single debuted at #28 on the Billboard Hot 100 and peaked at #9 the following week; \"Canadian Idiot\", a parody of Green Day's \"American Idiot\", also charted, peaking at #82."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/Soli4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straight_Outta_Lynwood"},{"title":"No Cigar","blocks":[{"text":"No Cigar is an EP by Swedish punk rock band Millencolin, released on 8 May 2001 by Burning Heart Records in Sweden, Epitaph Records in North America, and Shock Records in Australia. It appears as the opening track from their fourth album Pennybridge Pioneers (2000), where the track originated, and the EP itself is an extended single release. The North American release includes \"No Cigar\" as well as the tracks from the album's other two singles, \"Penguins & Polarbears\" and \"Fox\". In Australia, \"No Cigar\" was released as an enhanced CD single including the band's songs from their split EP with Midtown as well as four videos. \"No Cigar\" was also featured on the soundtrack to the video game Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 2 as well as the game's re-releases Tony Hawk's Pro Skater HD and Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 1 + 2. It is the third track on Epitaph Records' compilation Punk-O-Rama #5, released in 2000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/53/Millencolin_-_No_Cigar_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_Cigar"},{"title":"Cigar","blocks":[{"text":"A cigar is a rolled bundle of dried and fermented tobacco leaves made to be smoked. Cigars are produced in a variety of sizes and shapes. Since the 20th century, almost all cigars are made of three distinct components: the filler, the binder leaf which holds the filler together, and a wrapper leaf, which is often the highest quality leaf used. Often there will be a cigar band printed with the cigar manufacturer's logo. Modern cigars can come with two or more bands, especially Cuban cigars, showing Limited Edition bands displaying the year of production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg/330px-Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cigar"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Chamillionaire_July_2008.jpg/500px-Chamillionaire_July_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Chamillionaire_July_2008.jpg/1280px-Chamillionaire_July_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Chamillionaire_July_2008.jpg/500px-Chamillionaire_July_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChamillionaire_July_2008.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/RiP2013_GreenDay_Billie_Joe_Armstrong_0022.jpg/500px-RiP2013_GreenDay_Billie_Joe_Armstrong_0022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/RiP2013_GreenDay_Billie_Joe_Armstrong_0022.jpg/1280px-RiP2013_GreenDay_Billie_Joe_Armstrong_0022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/RiP2013_GreenDay_Billie_Joe_Armstrong_0022.jpg/500px-RiP2013_GreenDay_Billie_Joe_Armstrong_0022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARiP2013_GreenDay_Billie_Joe_Armstrong_0022.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Atlantic_record_sucks_shirt_your_pitiful_aug_8th_2007_ohio_state_fair.JPG/500px-Atlantic_record_sucks_shirt_your_pitiful_aug_8th_2007_ohio_state_fair.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Atlantic_record_sucks_shirt_your_pitiful_aug_8th_2007_ohio_state_fair.JPG/1280px-Atlantic_record_sucks_shirt_your_pitiful_aug_8th_2007_ohio_state_fair.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia